{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Chi21GarsideZero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Chi21GarsideZero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi21_garside_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi21_garside_zero","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Chi21GarsideZero.lean#L106-L143","doc":"**α₃-break structural prune.**  The `(2,1)` Hecke character of the\nGarside half-twist `σ₁σ₂σ₁` vanishes, derived from the explicit\n`2 × 2` Hoefsmit seminormal matrices:\n\n  `χ^{(2,1)}(σ₁σ₂σ₁) = tr ρ_{(2,1)}(σ₁σ₂σ₁) = a₁²·a₋₂ + a₋₁²·a₂ = 0`.\n\nOver any field, with `q ≠ 0`, `q² ≠ 1`, and `q⁴ ≠ 1` (the\nseminormal axial-distance denominators nonzero).  The off-diagonal\nseminormal entry `b` is arbitrary — it does not enter the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rhoGarside","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rhoGarside","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Chi21GarsideZero.lean#L100-L104","doc":"`ρ_{(2,1)}(σ₁σ₂σ₁)`, the seminormal representation of the Garside\n(half-twist) element `Δ = σ₁σ₂σ₁ ∈ B₃`, evaluated in the `(2,1)`\nblock. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rhoSigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rhoSigma2","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Chi21GarsideZero.lean#L95-L98","doc":"`ρ_{(2,1)}(σ₂)` — the `t₁ ↔ t₂` mixing block; `b` is the\n(undetermined) seminormal off-diagonal entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rhoSigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rhoSigma1","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Chi21GarsideZero.lean#L91-L93","doc":"`ρ_{(2,1)}(σ₁)` — diagonal on the standard-tableau basis `{t₁,t₂}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.aNeg2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.aNeg2","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Chi21GarsideZero.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.a2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.a2","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Chi21GarsideZero.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.aNeg1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.aNeg1","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Chi21GarsideZero.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.a1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.a1","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/Chi21GarsideZero.lean#L81-L86","doc":"The Hoefsmit seminormal diagonal entry `a_ρ = (q − q⁻¹)/(1 − q^{−2ρ})`\nfor the small axial distances used by the `(2,1)` irrep of `H₃(q)`.\nStated over a generic field per the base-ring convention (§7c); no\narchimedean structure is required — `q` is a formal parameter with\nthe seminormal denominators kept nonzero by hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}